course: dictionary
lesson: 5434
title: A word from faraway Tibet
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You do not need to know every word to understand a text. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they are its context and they give clues. The word lama is not explained in the sentence below, so you must use the other clues and the lesson to find its meaning.
explain: «Tibet came under the control of the People's Republic in 1950–1951; the Chinese government says Tibet has been part of China for centuries, while the Dalai Lama and many Tibetans abroad describe it as historically independent or self-governing.» The Dalai Lama is named as an important person whose view is reported. Words like «says» and «describe» show that people are giving their own views, so the sentence is reporting different opinions.
explain: Lama comes from Tibetan Buddhism. A lama is a teacher or monk, and Buddhists believe a lama guides people on the path to wisdom and kindness. When context is not enough, check a dictionary. Then try your meaning in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: «Lama» means a teacher or monk in Tibetan Buddhism.
fact: The Dalai Lama is the most famous lama, a spiritual leader of Tibetan Buddhists.
fact: Buddhists believe a lama guides people on the path to wisdom and kindness.
fact: Lamas often live and pray in monasteries, and they may use prayer wheels.
fact: Context clues like «says» and «describe» can show you that people are giving different views.
exercise: What is a lama? | A mountain in Tibet | A wheel used to pray | A kind of Tibetan food | *A teacher or monk in Tibetan Buddhism
exercise: Buddhists believe a lama guides people on the path to what? | Speed and strength | *Wisdom and kindness | Winning every game | Riches and fame
exercise: In «the Dalai Lama and many Tibetans abroad describe it as historically independent», what does abroad mean? | Under the ground | *In other countries, away from home | Very old and dusty | Inside a monastery
test: The Dalai Lama is the most famous lama. What kind of leader is he? | *A spiritual leader of Tibetan Buddhists | A king of China | A football coach | A park ranger
test: Where might lamas live and pray with prayer wheels? | *In a monastery | On a space station | At the bottom of a swimming pool | At a seaside café
exam: In «the Dalai Lama and many Tibetans abroad describe it as historically independent», which word shows that these people are giving their own view? | China | Tibet | centuries | *describe
